From: CachyOS-ARM64 port overlay <builder@local>
Date: Wed, 08 Oct 2026
Subject: [PATCH] remoteproc: qcom_q6v5: resolve leftover merge conflict in request_stop

The branch head (3f0d8691 "Ubuntu: Update changelog to 7.3-rc3-jg-0")
contains an unresolved version-control conflict in
drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5.c: qcom_q6v5_request_stop() carried both
sides of a merge between local crash-flow changes and upstream commit
0ca7f0fc41200 ("remoteproc: qcom_q6v5: Send SMP2P stop signal in
attached/detached state").

Resolution: keep the HEAD side:

  /* A watchdog/fatal IRQ clears running; logical crashes still need a stop. */
  if (!was_running || qcom_sysmon_shutdown_acked(sysmon))
          return 0;

Rationale: with running=true the stop is sent in attached/detached states,
which is exactly the upstream commit's intent, while also honoring the
local requirement that logical crashes still receive a stop request.
The upstream variant (skip when state == RPROC_CRASHED) would suppress
that. The whole tree was scanned for conflict markers; this was the only
file affected.

Build error fixed:
  qcom_q6v5.c:275:1: error: version control conflict marker in file
  qcom_q6v5.c:281:9: error: invalid suffix 'ca7f0fc41200' on integer constant
---
 drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5.c | 6 +-----
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5.c b/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5.c
--- a/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5.c
+++ b/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5.c
@@ -272,13 +272,9 @@ int qcom_q6v5_request_stop(struct qcom_q6v5 *q6v5, struct qcom_sysmon *sysmon)
 
 	q6v5->running = false;
 
-<<<<<<< HEAD
 	/* A watchdog/fatal IRQ clears running; logical crashes still need a stop. */
 	if (!was_running || qcom_sysmon_shutdown_acked(sysmon))
-=======
-	/* Don't perform SMP2P dance if remote crashed or already stopped */
-	if (q6v5->rproc->state == RPROC_CRASHED || qcom_sysmon_shutdown_acked(sysmon))
->>>>>>> 0ca7f0fc41200 (remoteproc: qcom_q6v5: Send SMP2P stop signal in attached/detached state)
 		return 0;
 
 	qcom_smem_state_update_bits(q6v5->state,
